    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0429" n="1163" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1163"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Taylor.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June 11,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Instructions in Mora case mailed 6th instant with copy joint resolution of
                    Congress requesting President to insist upon payment of stipulated indemnity,
                    principal and interest. These instructions direct you, in event that Spain is
                    unable to pay the full amount at once, to urge an immediate payment on account,
                    end that arrangements be made for early payment of balance.</p>
                <p>See minister of foreign affairs and represent importance of satisfying this claim
                    irrespective of action on proposed claims convention. Press for settlement and
                    report by cable after receipt of said instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
